#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# root_sum

#% text
# `root_sum(x => p(x), x => g(x))` is the sum of `g(r)` over the roots `r` of the polynomial `p`, each counted with its multiplicity.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `p` is factored over the rational numbers. The roots of linear and quadratic factors are written with radicals; a factor of degree 3 or more stays as a `root_sum` over that factor, with integer coefficients.

#% item
# When `g` is a rational function of its argument, the sum over a factor of higher degree is computed exactly: a rational number, or a rational function when `g` has one other variable.

#% item
# `n` gives the numeric value: the sum over the numeric roots.

#% item
# `normal` writes the sum with root objects: `g(root(p, 1)) + ... + g(root(p, d))`.

#% item
# `d` differentiates the function inside the sum; the sum is over roots that do not depend on the variable.

#% item
# `integrate` gives a `root_sum` for the logarithmic part of a rational function when the residues are the roots of an irreducible polynomial of degree 3 or more; `to_radicals` writes cubics and quartics with radicals.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# The sum of the squares of the roots of a cubic:

#% cell
root_sum(x => x^3 + x + 1, x => x^2)
#% output
#= -2

#% text
# Quadratic factors are written with radicals:

#% cell
root_sum(x => x^2 - 2, x => x*log(z - x))
#% output
#= log(z - 2^(1/2))*2^(1/2) - log(z + 2^(1/2))*2^(1/2)

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# A sum over the roots of an irreducible cubic stays:

#% cell
root_sum(x => x^3 + x + 1, x => log(2 - x))
#% output
#= root_sum(x => 1 + x + x^3, x => log(2 - x))

#% text
# Its numeric value:

#% cell
n(root_sum(x => x^3 + x + 1, x => log(2 - x)))
#% output
#= 2.3978952727983702

#% text
# A rational function of the roots and another variable:

#% cell
root_sum(x => x^3 + x + 1, x => 1/(z - x))
#% output
#= (1 + 3*z^2)/(1 + z + z^3)

#% text
# `normal` writes the sum over root objects:

#% cell
normal(root_sum(x => x^3 + x + 7, x => sin(x)))
#% output
#= sin(root(&(7 + &1 + &1^3), 1)) + sin(root(&(7 + &1 + &1^3), 2)) + sin(root(&(7 + &1 + &1^3), 3))

#% text
# Repeated factors count with their multiplicity:

#% cell
root_sum(x => (x^3 + x + 1)^2, x => x^2)
#% output
#= -4

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# The antiderivative of a rational function whose residues need a cubic:

#% cell
integrate(1/(x^3 + x + 1), x)
#% output
#= root_sum(t => 1 + t + t^3, t => log(x - t)/(1 + 3*t^2))

#% text
# Its derivative is the integrand again:

#% cell
d(integrate(1/(x^3 + x + 1), x), x)
#% output
#= (1 + x + x^3)^-1

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `to_radicals`, `root`, `integrate`, `minimal_polynomial`
